{
  "title": "Neck Injuries in Athletes",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3114/neck-injuries-in-athletes",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 14 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Introduction",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Injuries to the cervical spine can occur in all sports and range from soft tissue injuries to quadriplegia",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "2",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "spectrum of injuries include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**ligament sprains in cervical spine**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**burners / stingers**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**spear tackler's spine**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3114/images/spear_tackler.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "definition",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "developmental narrowing (stenosis) of the cervical canal",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "persistent straightening or reversal of the normal cervical lordotic curve",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "concomitant posttraumatic roentgenographic abnormalities of the cervical spine",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "documentation of having employed spear tackling techniques",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "contraindication to play in contact sports",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**cervical fxs**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**transient quadriplegia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "neuropraxia of the cervical cord",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "bilateral upper and lower extremity pain, parasthesias, and weakness",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms resolve within minutes to hours",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**quadriplegia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Injuries to the cervical spine are primarily seen in contact sports",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "common among football and rugby players",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "evolution of protective gear has decreased incidence",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "axial load (compression) with flexion of the spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "most injuries in contact sports occur during tackling of another player",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**\"spear tackling\"**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**is the most common mechanism of neck injury in football**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**can lead to gradual cervical stenosis and loss of cervical lordosis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "underlying conditions of the cervical spine can increase the severity of neck injuries and be contraindications to play. They include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**previous trauma to cervical spine (**fractures, ligamentous injuries)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**cervical stenosis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**congenital odontoid hypoplasia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**os odontoideum**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**Klippel-Feil anomalies**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Cervical spine",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evaluate mental status",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "spinal injuries should be assumed in the athlete with loss of or altered consciousness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "neck pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "neurological symptoms such as numbness, tingling or weakness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam (on-field evaluation)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "when cervical spine injury is suspected in the field",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "stabilize the head and neck",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "log roll to supine position",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**remove facemask to protect airway as needed**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**recent NATA guidelines allow remove of both helmet and shoulder pads if it can be done safely**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "CPR as indicated",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "log roll place on backboard",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "transport to location to perform complete physical exam",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "look for deformities of cervical spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpate",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "spinous processes for step off or pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurological exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "muscle testing of all 4 extremities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "test sensation throughout extremities",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "test reflexes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "burner / stingers with recurring symptoms",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "neurologic symptoms and transient quadriplegia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "cervical spine trauma series",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "canal diameter of < 13mm (normal is ~17mm)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Torg-Pavlo ratio (canal/vertebral body width) of < 0.8 (normal is 1.0)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3114/images/xray-cervical-lateral_-_shows_torg_ratio_small.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Torg ratio is technique dependent, not predictive, and not accurate in large athletes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "bilateral neurologic symptoms",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "look for spinal stenosis or loss of CSF around the spinal cord",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "return to play criteria",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "burners/stingers",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "complete resolution of symptoms",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "normal strength and range of motion",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "transient quadriplegia with normal MRI findings",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "congenital stenosis (Torg-Pavlov ratio <0.8) without instability (but patients should be counseled regarding the risks)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "NO return to play (contraindications to RTP)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "transient quadriplegia with severe stenosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "spear tackler's spine",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "cervical neuropraxia with ligamentous instability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "upper C spine abnormalities (C0 to C2) are absolute contraindications for RTP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**odontoid hypoplasia**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**os odontoideum**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "**atlantooccipital fusion**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Torg 1 Klippel-Feil anomaly (long fusion mass) absolute contraindication to play",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Torg 2 Klippel-Feil (only 1 or 2 segments) with limited motion, secondary degenerative changes or instability",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Torg 2 Klippel-Feil below C3, asymptomatic, is a relative contraindication to RTP",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "asymptomatic athletes with no T2-signal change following a 3-level ACDF",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "solid 1- or 2-level ACDF ok to RTP, as long as asymptomatic with no T2-signal change",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "solid 1-level ACDF with continued T2-signal changes can be considered on case-by-case basis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "treatment is the same as for other traumatic injuries to the spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
